# Financial Integrity

- Ledger is the source of truth; balances are projections.
- Monetary values use integer minor units or safe decimal with explicit currency.
- Never use binary floating point for financial math.
- Never update historical commission/payout truth in place to "fix" history.
- Corrections are compensating entries with actor, reason and references.
- Preserve commission rate/rule snapshots.
- Commission holds remain independently timestamped.
- Payout reservation is atomic and race-safe.
- Refund/chargeback effects follow explicit state transitions.
- Payment webhook event IDs and idempotency keys are unique and deduplicated.
- Reconciliation jobs compare payment -> invoice -> commission -> payout.
- Financial mismatches are high-severity operational events.
- Sensitive financial actions require explicit permissions and immutable audit entries.
